agg ThreeDice dfreq [3] dsev [1:6] note{Sum of three dice -- exact discrete aggregate; zero validation error.} tags{topic:aggregate, role:intro, check:independent-oracle}
doc{{{
## Problem

You want to see what `aggregate` computes on something you can check in your
head. Three dice: a fixed frequency of 3, a severity uniform on 1..6.

## Solution

```python
a = build('''<<decl>>''')
qd(a.summary_df)
```

## Discussion

Everything here is discrete and lands exactly on the grid, so this is the one
case where the FFT is not an approximation at all -- the aggregate PMF is the
exact three-fold convolution of the die. That is why it is the first recipe: it
separates "is the method right" from "is the discretization fine", which every
later recipe has to hold apart.

`dfreq [3]` is an explicit outcome list with a single outcome, so N = 3 with
probability one. `dsev [1:6]` is the inclusive range 1, 2, ..., 6 with equal
weights.

## Check

```python
# E[A] = 3 x 3.5 = 10.5, and the estimate is EXACT, not merely close
assert abs(a.actual_m - 10.5) < 1e-12
assert abs(a.est_m - 10.5) < 1e-9
# support runs 3..18; each extreme has probability (1/6)^3
assert abs(a.density_df.loc[3, 'p_total'] - (1 / 6) ** 3) < 1e-12
assert abs(a.density_df.loc[18, 'p_total'] - (1 / 6) ** 3) < 1e-12
```
}}};
agg ThreeDiceSum dfreq [3] dsev [1:6] note{Sum of the rolls of three dice.} tags{topic:aggregate};
agg TweedieCompound tweedie 1 1.005 0.1 note{Tweedie by mean, power p, and dispersion (variance = dispersion * mean**p).} tags{topic:aggregate};
agg TweedieDirect 10.050251256281404 claims sev gamma 0.0995 cv 0.07088812050083283 poisson note{Tweedie defined by claim count, gamma mean and cv} tags{topic:aggregate};
agg TweedieDispersion tweedie 1 1.005 0.1 note{Tweedie defined using mean, p, and dispersion, variance = dispersion xs mean**p} tags{topic:aggregate};
agg TweedieFromMoments 10.050251256281404 claims sev 0.0005 * gamma 199 poisson note{Tweedie defined by claim count, gamma scale and shape} tags{topic:aggregate};
agg TweedieSimple tweedie 1 1.005 0.1 note{Tweedie via mean, p, dispersion; variance = dispersion * mean**p.} tags{topic:aggregate};

